Example 16: a model in an Apptainer container, run by an execution server.

The workflow (Example16.py) gives its model only by ID ("mupif-example16"). Its package names a
container image (Runtime Type = "apptainer"): the execution server (server.py) copies the image into
its package cache, verifies it against the digest in the manifest, and runs the model with
"apptainer exec": the package is mounted at /mupif/package, the job's work directory at its own
path, the network is the host's.

Requirements: Apptainer (or Singularity) on the server host, with unprivileged user namespaces for
building the image (apptainer build --fakeroot); network access on the first build.

    python make_package.py        # image.sif (a few minutes the first time) and package/
    python ../runns.py &          # nameserver (or use an existing one: MUPIF_NS)
    python server.py &
    python Example16.py

With mupifDB as the registry: python -m mupif.modelpackage publish package (admin account in
API_CREDENTIALS_FILE, MUPIFDB_REST_SERVER), then start server.py with MUPIFDB_REST_SERVER set.

The image is referenced by its file path (a shared file system on several hosts). In a real
deployment it would be pushed to an OCI registry and referenced pinned by digest:
    apptainer push image.sif oras://ghcr.io/<org>/<name>:1.0
    Image = "oras://ghcr.io/<org>/<name>@sha256:<digest>"
